<title>JAPAN: Deutsche Telekom debuts at 2,500 yen.</title>
<headline>Deutsche Telekom debuts at 2,500 yen.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-11-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>German telecommunications giant Deutsche Telekom  9496.T made its debut on the foreign section of the Tokyo Stock Exchange at 2,500 yen on Tuesday morning amid active trade.  </p>
<p>The shares were first listed on the Frankfurt stock exchange priced at 28.5 marks. They started trade on Monday at a 16.5 percent premium and closed at 33.90 marks, with about 38 million shares traded.</p>
<p>Trade on Wall Street was also heady, with the issue closing 14 percent higher at 2-39/64 above the $21-1/2 pricing and 17 million shares traded.</p>
<p>At 0016 GMT in Tokyo, Deutsche Telekom share turnover was 2.912 million shares.</p>
